parts.text:
Answers:
1. 千焦: real conversion ×4.184
2. Animation: home page only
3. Animation form: staggered element-by-element fade-in (逐个错峰渐显)

Now design the plan:

## 1. 启动动画（index.ux，逐个错峰渐显）
- Elements: title, title-accent, sub, btn (开始游戏), btn2 (更多数据), btn3 (设置) — 6 elements. Maybe settings panel doesn't need it (it's if-gated).
- Each element gets opacity binding: `style="opacity:{{ oTitle }}"` etc. — 6 bindings.
- Stagger: each element fades in over ~150-200ms with 60-80ms delay between starts. Total within 0.5s.
- Implementation pure JS: recursive setTimeout chain or one setTimeout per element. Simplest: array of steps scheduled with setTimeout:
```js
onInit() {
  ...
  this.introFade()
},
introFade() {
  var self = this
  // staggered: each element starts at i*70ms, 10 steps of 20ms
  var keys = ['oTitle', 'oAccent', 'oSsub', 'oBtn1', 'oBtn2', 'oBtn3']
  ...
}
```
Simpler per-element: use one shared stepping function:
```js
introFade() {
  var self = this
  var seq = [
    ['oTitle', 0], ['oAccent', 70], ['oSub', 140],
    ['oBtn1', 210], ['oBtn2', 280], ['oBtn3', 350]
  ]
  for (var i = 0; i < seq.length; i++) {
    (function(k, delay) {
      setTimeout(function() { self.fadeIn(k) }, delay)
    })(seq[i][0], seq[i][1])
  }
},
fadeIn(key) {
  var self = this
  var step = function() {
    var v = self[key] + 0.2
    if (v >= 1) { self[key] = 1; return }
    self[key] = v
    setTimeout(step, 30)   // 5 steps × 30ms = 150ms per element
  }
  step()
}
```
Timing: last element starts at 350ms, finishes at 500ms. Total = 0.5s.But careful: 6 elements × 5 setTimeouts = 30 timeouts over 0.5s — trivial. And these are one-shot, no leak. Also `self[key]` — private fields must be declared: oTitle, oAccent, oSub, oBtn1, oBtn2, oBtn3 (each 0 initial).

Template bindings: add `style="opacity:{{ oTitle }}"` to title text, accent div, sub text, btn, btn2, btn3. Note some elements already have class-based styling; opacity in inline style is fine.

Initial opacity 0 → invisible at start. If JS fails, elements stay invisible — risk! Mitigation: safety timeout setting all to 1 after 600ms regardless. Or initial 1 and start fade from 0... Actually setting initial 0 and stepping up is standard; add a fallback `setTimeout(all to 1, 800)` for safety. Good practice on embedded.

## 2. 挡板碰壁涟漪（game.ux）
Edge-detection flags `_pwL`, `_pwR` (plain fields):
In tick(), after paddle clamp:
```js
if (this.px <= this.playL) {
  if (!this._pwL) { this._pwL = true; this.spawnRipple(this.playL, this.py + this.ph / 2) }
} else {
  this._pwL = false
}
if (this.px >= this.playR - this.pw) {
  if (!this._pwR) { this._pwR = true; this.spawnRipple(this.playR, this.py + this.ph / 2) }
} else {
  this._pwR = false
}
```
Reuses ripple pool (3 slots shared with ball wall hits, pool-full drops). Also reset flags in resetBall (`this._pwL = false; this._pwR = false`) — actually not strictly needed since flags only suppress repeat; but if game restarts while paddle at wall... resetBall sets px to center, so next tick flags reset naturally. Fine to add reset anyway for cleanliness. Also init in setupKeys.

