Now the _tickFn chain protection. Current _tickFn (from earlier reads):

```js
      this._tickFn = function() {
        self.timer = null
        if (self.state === 0 && !self.paused) {
          var now = Date.now()
          if (self._lastTick) {
            if (now - self._lastTick > 300) {
              self._slowFrames++
              if (self._slowFrames >= 10) {
                self._lastTick = 0
                self.autoPause()
                return
              }
            } else {
              self._slowFrames = 0
            }
          }
          self._lastTick = now
          self.tick()
        }
        if (self.state === 0 && !self.paused) self.schedule()
      }
```

Note: the autoPause path does `return` — skipping the schedule at the end (intentional: paused). With the new design "无论异常与否都继续调度" — but autoPause sets paused=true, and the final `if (self.state === 0 && !self.paused) self.schedule()` won't schedule when paused. Good.

